+Form on a unit interval. For \(t\in[k,k+1]\), \(W_t=\sum_{j<k}B^{(j)}_1+B^{(k)}_{t-k}\). At \(t=k+1\) this agrees with the formula for the next interval, because \(B^{(k+1)}_0=0\) by (D1). So on each \([k,k+1]\) the path of \(W\) is a constant plus a path of \(B^{(k)}\), the pieces agree at the integers, and \(W\) is continuous. Also \(W_0=B^{(0)}_0=0\), which is (D1).
